<http://data.silknow.org/object/90f9ef1f-b2c9-32d2-b8e1-3bf9f9ef2953/observation/3>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Wide skirts were a focal feature of fashion during this period. By 1865 the fullness of the skirt had receded towards the back of the garment creating a flatter front. Women wore crinoline petticoats made of steel hoops under their dresses to give them this distinctive shape. Lightweight dress fabrics such as silk and muslin were popular as they draped gracefully  over the crinoline cage."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/90f9ef1f-b2c9-32d2-b8e1-3bf9f9ef2953> .

